WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.515
Lesson 13.5.

00:00:02.515 --> 00:00:05.370
Scaling, compounding and the annual review.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:07.413
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:07.413 --> 00:00:09.733
able to grow the engine safely and review

00:00:09.733 --> 00:00:11.445
it like a bank's annual report.

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:14.035
Here's the plan.

00:00:14.035 --> 00:00:15.720
First, the key ideas.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.245
Then, your checklist.

00:00:17.245 --> 00:00:19.407
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:20.707 --> 00:00:23.782
Compounding: reinvesting the retained share grows

00:00:23.782 --> 00:00:25.927
principal, and income with it.

00:00:25.927 --> 00:00:29.852
At a 4.66% risk-adjusted yield with 30%

00:00:29.852 --> 00:00:35.647
retained, principal grows ~1.4%/yr from retention alone.

00:00:35.647 --> 00:00:41.107
The payout grows at about the same rate: $16,310

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:47.312
→ ~$17,480 after five years (before any new capital).

00:00:47.312 --> 00:00:50.071
Scaling rules as the book grows: Check pool

00:00:50.071 --> 00:00:52.942
depth and exit liquidity at the new size.

00:00:52.942 --> 00:00:57.075
Annual review (one page): First, Caps are percentages, so

00:00:57.075 --> 00:01:00.725
position sizes rise, and so does market impact.

00:01:00.725 --> 00:01:03.693
Next, Add independent protocols and issuers

00:01:03.693 --> 00:01:06.422
before adding size to existing ones.

00:01:06.422 --> 00:01:08.983
Then, more size means more value at

00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:11.987
stake in custody: revisit Module 12.2.

00:01:11.987 --> 00:01:16.847
Also, Balance sheet: start vs end equity, LTV, runway.

00:01:16.847 --> 00:01:18.660
On top of that, Income:

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.077
expected vs realised, by source.

00:01:22.378 --> 00:01:25.853
And Losses and near-misses: what happened, what changed.

00:01:25.853 --> 00:01:28.463
Plus, Payout: paid vs policy.

00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:30.924
One more: Risk assumptions: update loss

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.686
probabilities from the year's incidents.

00:01:33.686 --> 00:01:36.531
And finally, Custody and succession drill: done?

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.291
Here's your checklist.

00:01:39.291 --> 00:01:40.826
Do it now, for real.

00:01:40.826 --> 00:01:44.171
First, Retained income reinvested per policy.

00:01:44.171 --> 00:01:47.111
Next, Exit liquidity checked at current size.

00:01:47.111 --> 00:01:49.261
And finally, Annual review completed

00:01:49.261 --> 00:01:50.714
and filed with the books.

00:01:52.014 --> 00:01:53.224
Question 1.

00:01:53.224 --> 00:01:56.254
Yield 5%, 40% retained.

00:01:56.254 --> 00:01:57.784
Growth from retention alone?

00:02:02.204 --> 00:02:04.309
The answer: ~2% a year.

00:02:05.609 --> 00:02:06.854
Question 2.

00:02:06.854 --> 00:02:09.309
Why check exit liquidity as the book grows?

00:02:13.729 --> 00:02:17.639
The answer: A position that was easy to exit

00:02:17.639 --> 00:02:20.854
at $50k may move the market at $500k.

00:02:22.154 --> 00:02:23.424
Question 3.

00:02:23.424 --> 00:02:25.249
What should the annual review update?

00:02:29.669 --> 00:02:32.415
The answer: Loss-probability assumptions, from

00:02:32.415 --> 00:02:34.576
the year's incidents and near-misses.

00:02:35.876 --> 00:02:37.121
Let's recap.

00:02:37.121 --> 00:02:39.877
Caps are percentages, so position sizes

00:02:39.877 --> 00:02:42.381
rise, and so does market impact.

00:02:42.381 --> 00:02:45.284
Add independent protocols and issuers before

00:02:45.284 --> 00:02:47.455
adding size to existing ones.

00:02:47.455 --> 00:02:50.740
More size means more value at stake in custody.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:54.580
Balance sheet: start vs end equity, LTV, runway.

00:02:55.879 --> 00:02:58.394
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:58.394 --> 00:03:01.769
Next up, Lesson 14.0: Mastery Starter.
